      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1376076118,
      "text": "Satureja montana, is a perennial, semi-evergreen herb in the family Lamiaceae, native to warm temperate regions of southern Europe, the Mediterranean, and Africa. It has dark green leaves and summer flowers ranging from pale lavender, pink to white. The closely related summer savory is an annual plant."
